s, or a sharp shift in the national political environment, could move the margin substantially.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Connecticut enters the 2028 presidential race as a Democratic-leaning state, with a partisan lean of eight points toward Democrats. The incumbent Republican president is term-limited, making this an open contest between nominees to be determined, and no general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet. Headlines so far center on the Democratic primary field, including Senator Chris Murphy's national ambitions, rather than on the general election itself.\n\nWith no state-specific polling, the forecast rests on Connecticut's partisan fundamentals. The state has reliably backed Democrats in recent presidential cycles, and the available evidence points to a Democratic advantage of roughly eight points. Uncertainty remains wide given the absence of direct polling this early in the cycle. Early fundraising, the resolution of each party's nomination, and the first general-election surveys will be the main signals as the race develops.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8243, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.781, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7754, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7738, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7768, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7811, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7718, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7751, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p